ger bar.\n  16: \n  17:     Input structure\n  18:     - The grid has one dominant background color and exactly two foreground colors.\n  19:     - One foreground color forms many vertical one-cell-wide bars; the other appears as a single vertical marker segment.\n  20:     - The marker segment occupies exactly the top or bottom half of its containing vertical bar.\n  21:     Rule\n  22:     - Recolor the current marker segment back to the bar color.\n  23:     - Find the unique all-bar-color vertical bar whose height is two pixels greater than the marked source bar.\n  24:     - Recolor the same half of that next longer bar to the marker color.\n  25:     Key insight\n  26:     - Each bar's total height encodes an ordered size, and the marker advances from a 2k bar to the corresponding 2(k+1) bar while preserving whether it marks the top or bottom half.\n  27:     \"\"\"\n  28:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n  29:     assert g.ndim == 2\n  30: \n  31:     bg = int(get_bg(g))\n  32:     colors = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})\n  33:     assert len(colors) == 2, f\"expected exactly two foreground colors, got {colors}\"\n  34: \n  35:     mono_component_counts = {\n  36:         int(color): len(\n  37:             find_components(\n  38:                 g,\n  39:                 bg=bg,\n  40:                 colors=[int(color)],\n  41:                 connectivity=4,\n  42:                 monochromatic=True,\n  43:             )\n  44:         )\n  45:         for color in colors\n  46:     }\n  47:     marker_colors = [color for color, count in mono_component_counts.items() if count == 1]\n  48:     assert len(marker_colors) == 1, f\"expected one single-component marker color, got {mono_component_counts}\"\n  49:     marker_color = int(marker_colors[0])\n  50: \n  51:     bar_colors = [int(color) for color in colors if int(color) != marker_color]\n  52:     assert len(bar_colors) == 1\n  53:     bar_color = int(bar_colors[0])\n  54: \n  55:     marker_compone