{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/17/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"da515329\" lines=\"11-24\">\n<description>\nGrow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross centered in the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Each arm tip launches a \"turtle\" heading 90° right of its outward direction.\n- Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).\n- Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.\n- Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.\n\nKey insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"6e4f6532\" lines=\"26-41\">\n<description>\nDock train sprites onto station groups by matching coupler count, then orient via divider-color markers.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg; colored stripes (edge + internal) partition grid into rectangular regions.\n- Color 8 forms train bodies; color 9 marks both isolated stations and train-attached couplers.\n- Stripe-colored pixels on trains are orientation markers.\n\nRule:\n- Stations = 8-connected 9-clusters not adjacent to any 8. Trains = components containing 8.\n- Match train to station group where |couplers| == |station size|.\n- Rotate/flip train so marker pixels face the same-color boundary stripe of the target region.\n- Translate so couplers align exactly onto station cells; erase original position.\n\nKey insight: Coupler count selects the docking target; marker color encodes which boundary stripe to face, fixing the unique orientation.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a1aa0c1e\" lines=\"74-97\">\n<description>\nCompress the stacked colored bars into a compact ordered table with the control pixel on the selected row.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid contains several full-width colored bars from top to\n  bottom; the last bar is the base/separator color.\n- Each non-base bar may have an aligned three-column comb motif below it,\n  alternating side-pair rows with solid rows.\n- A singleton control pixel sits away from the colored motifs.\n\nRule\n- Make one output row per non-base bar, preserving top-to-bottom order.\n- In that row, paint the bar color once for each solid three-pixel row in\n  its motif, then paint the base-bar color in the separator column.\n- The singleton control pixel sits immediately above the base bar. Among\n  motifs whose open side-pair parity is compatible with that bottom row,\n  put the control pixel in the output row with the fewest solid rows; use\n  horizontal distance to the motif center only to break count ties.\n\nKey insight\n- The vertical comb height is a count, while the control pixel is read by\n  projecting it onto the center gap of compatible comb rows rather than by\n  its vertical band alone.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"182e5d0f\" lines=\"89-103\">\n<description>\nMove each gray marker along its green path until it reaches the cell next to a black-green-black gate, erasing the path behind it.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Foreground components are made from a path color, a paired gate-end color, and single marker pixels.\n- A gate is a straight end-center-end motif whose center has the path color and whose two ends share the gate-end color.\n\nRule:\n- In every 4-connected foreground component with exactly one marker and one gate, erase the marker and all path-color pixels except the gate center.\n- Place the marker on the unique path-color pixel adjacent to the gate center but not between the two gate ends.\n- Components without both a marker and a gate stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The black-green-black motif marks the stopping gate; the gray marker consumes the connected green path until it rests on the path cell immediately beside that gate.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a47bf94d\" lines=\"178-189\">\n<description>\nTransmit colored tokens along wire networks, converting each to its complementary 3×3 pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. Non-bg cells form wire networks and 3×3 tokens (solid blocks or X/diagonal patterns) near wire endpoints.\n\nRule:\n- Every solid 3×3 token is replaced in-place by a diamond (center + 4 cardinal neighbors).\n- Each token near a wire endpoint sends its complement to the opposite endpoint: solid emits X, X emits diamond.\n\nKey insight: Token shape cycles solid → X → diamond; wires route each complement to the far end.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"1818057f\" lines=\"6-19\">\n<description>\nDetect thin '+' shapes in a single foreground color and recolor them to teal.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- One foreground color (e.g. yellow) forms various shapes on the bg, some of which are small '+' crosses.\n\nRule:\n- A '+' center is any foreground pixel whose 4 orthogonal neighbors are also foreground.\n- Recolor each such center and its 4 neighbors to teal (8).\n- All other pixels remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight: Only compact 5-cell crosses qualify — a pixel embedded in a larger filled region also satisfies the neighbor check, so the rule highlights every local '+' motif, not just isolated ones.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"f931b4a8\" lines=\"10-27\">\n<description>\nCount the two upper quadrant control regions to size an output made from the lower quadrant pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is an even square split into four equal quadrants.\n- Black is the background.\n- The upper-left and upper-right quadrants are control regions.\n- The lower-left quadrant is a color source tile; the lower-right quadrant is either a stencil tile or empty.\n\nRule:\n- Output height is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-left quadrant.\n- Output width is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-right quadrant.\n- If the lower-right stencil has foreground pixels, tile it over the output; each stencil background pixel is filled from the lower-left quadrant cell at the corresponding coarse tile position.\n- If the lower-right stencil is empty, tile the lower-left quadrant directly over the output.\n\nKey insight:\n- The top quadrants specify only dimensions, while the bottom quadrants specify a two-level repeated pattern: a fine stencil and coarse fill colors.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"271d71e2\" lines=\"9-22\">\n<description>\nMove bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.\n- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.\n\nRule:\n- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.\n- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).\n- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.\n\nKey insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"880c1354\" lines=\"14-28\">\n<description>\nRecolor the separated outer regions by rotating their colors one step clockwise around the yellow-orange divider.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid contains a fixed yellow/orange divider structure.\n- All other colors form separated 4-connected monochrome regions around that divider.\n\nRule:\n- Leave the yellow and orange pixels unchanged.\n- Sort the non-divider regions by their centroid angle around the divider centroid in screen-coordinate clockwise order.\n- Each region keeps its cells and receives the color of the previous region in that cyclic order.\n\nKey insight:\n- The objects do not move; only the color labels cycle through the spatial order of the regions around the divider.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"fc7cae8d\" lines=\"9-21\">\n<description>\nAlign a central rectangle to two colored frame-edge controls via rotation/reflection.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg grid with two solid-colored border edges (distinct non-bg colors).\n- A central filled rectangle with 1px colored guide edges on two sides, colors matching the frame controls.\n\nRule:\n- Rotate/mirror the object so its guide edges face the same sides as the matching frame controls.\n- Crop off the 1px guide edges from aligned sides.\n\nKey insight: Guide-edge colors encode target frame sides; the correct dihedral transform matches both simultaneously.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"984d8a3e\" lines=\"5-21\">\n<description>\nShift each row's dominant middle-color run left until its right edge aligns with the leftmost original right edge, moving displaced left-side pixels after the run.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has three colors.\n- The most common color forms one contiguous horizontal run in every row.\n- Pixels before those runs share one side color, and pixels after those runs share the other side color.\n\nRule:\n- Find the minimum right edge column among the middle-color runs.\n- In each row, keep the run width and the trailing right-side color count.\n- Place the middle-color run so its right edge is at that minimum column, unless the run is too wide, in which case start it at column 0.\n- Fill any remaining non-trailing cells with the left-side color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe varying row prefixes are movable padding; the stable feature is the leftmost right boundary of the middle-color shape.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"52df9849\" lines=\"49-67\">\n<description>\nComplete each partially hidden simple foreground shape by recoloring the occluding pixels in its footprint.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background and several solid foreground shapes.\n- Some shapes are partially hidden by other foreground colors, but their full\n  footprint is still indicated by a foreground-filled bbox or by a foreground-\n  filled 45-degree diagonal line.\n\nRule\n- For each foreground color, complete its full rectangular bbox when that bbox\n  contains no background and includes other colors.\n- Otherwise, complete its 45-degree diagonal line when all visible pixels lie\n  on that line and the hidden line cells are foreground, not background.\n- Recolor only those hidden footprint pixels; leave all other pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The occluded cells are exactly the non-background cells inside a simple\n  shape's implied footprint, so completing shapes is a local recoloring problem.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"50c07299\" lines=\"8-21\">\n<description>\nMove the diagonal foreground segment to the next longer run along the same up-right diagonal.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/17/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内部的孔洞形状匹配外部颜色图例，再用匹配到的颜色填充该区域的边框。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中散布着若干由灰色像素围成的封闭矩形区域，每个区域内部有一个由背景色构成的小型孔洞（孔洞形状各异，如 L 形、T 形、直线等）。网格边缘或角落处有一组颜色图例：每个图例由一个与孔洞形状相同的小型黑色图案和紧邻的一个彩色像素组成，彩色像素表示该形状对应的颜色。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 识别每个灰色封闭矩形内部的孔洞形状。\n  - 在颜色图例中找到与该孔洞形状全等（允许旋转和翻转匹配）的图案。\n  - 将该封闭矩形的灰色边框全部重新着色为图例中对应的彩色颜色。\n  - 孔洞本身保持为黑色不变，图例区域保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：需要先从区域内部提取孔洞的几何形状，再与外部图例进行形状匹配（含旋转/翻转），最后才能确定每个区域的目标颜色。形状匹配和颜色映射构成两层非平凡推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：沿每个箭头指示的方向将箭头尖端前方的彩色像素条\"推入\"相邻的空框中，使像素条按顺序填入框内对应行或列。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个由蓝色像素构成的空心矩形框（内部为黑色）。每个框的某一侧外部有一个由红色像素绘制的箭头（箭头由一条 3 像素的直线段加上尖端两侧各一个像素构成，形如 \">\" 或 \"v\" 等指向框的方向）。箭头与框之间夹着一列或一行彩色像素（颜色各异，非黑非蓝非红），像素数量恰好等于框沿箭头方向的深度。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 确定每个箭头的指向方向（上/下/左/右）。\n  - 将箭头与框之间的彩色像素条沿箭头方向依次\"推入\"框内：第一个像素填入框内最靠近箭头一侧的整行或整列，第二个像素填入下一行或列，依此类推。\n  - 填入时，每个像素的颜色覆盖该行/列中框内原本为黑色的所有像素位置。\n  - 箭头和原始彩色像素条在输出中被擦除（变为黑色），蓝色框边界保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：箭头方向决定填充轴向，彩色像素条的排列顺序决定框内逐层填充的颜色分配。解题者需要同时推断箭头方向解读规则和像素条到框内行列的映射关系。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将散落在网格中的彩色碎片按颜色配对，用两块碎片拼合还原各自所属的完整矩形，再将矩形移动到网格中同色锚点标记的位置。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干彩色碎片，每种非背景颜色恰好出现两块碎片。每块碎片是一个矩形的某个角落部分（即完整矩形被沿一条阶梯线切割后的其中一半）。同色的两块碎片可以无重叠、无间隙地拼合成一个完整的实心矩形。此外，网格中还有若干孤立的单像素锚点，每个锚点的颜色与某一对碎片相同，每种颜色恰好一个锚点。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每种颜色，找到两块同色碎片，确定它们拼合成完整矩形的唯一方式（一块碎片需要平移，不旋转，使两块碎片的阶梯切割边完美对齐）。\n  - 将拼合后的完整矩形平移，使矩形的左上角对齐到该颜色的锚点像素位置。\n  - 擦除碎片原始位置，在新位置绘制完整矩形。锚点像素被矩形覆盖。\n- `Key insight`：需要先通过碎片边缘的互补阶梯形状判断哪两块同色碎片如何拼合（这是第一层空间推理），然后再根据锚点确定放置位置（第二层映射推理）。碎片的阶梯切割线是拼合方式唯一性的关键。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在网格中，每个彩色种子像素沿其所在通道生长出与通道宽度匹配的色带，色带在遇到交叉口时根据交叉口中心标记的颜色决定转向方向。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有由灰色像素构成的通道网络，通道宽度为 1 或 2 个像素，通道之间以直角相交形成交叉口。每个交叉口的中心有一个彩色标记像素（非灰非黑）。通道的某些末端（死胡同处）有一个彩色种子像素，种子颜色与某个交叉口标记颜色相同。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 从每个种子像素出发，沿通道向内延伸，将通道中的灰色像素重新着色为种子的颜色，形成色带。\n  - 色带沿通道前进直到遇到交叉口。在交叉口处，找到与种子颜色相同的标记像素：若标记在交叉口的左侧通道方向，则色带左转；若在右侧方向，则右转；若在正前方，则直行。\n  - 色带穿过交叉口后继续沿新方向前进，直到遇到下一个交叉口（重复转向判断）或到达另一个死胡同为止。\n  - 交叉口标记像素本身被色带覆盖。若两条色带在同一通道段相遇，先到者（路径更短者）占据该段。\n- `Key insight`：种子颜色与交叉口标记颜色的匹配关系决定了每个交叉口的转向选择。解题者需要先建立\"颜色-转向方向\"的对应关系（第一层），再追踪色带沿通道网络的完整路径（第二层），最后处理多条色带的优先级冲突（第三层）。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：识别网格中每个多色拼图块的\"缺失角\"方位，将拼图块旋转使缺失角统一朝向同一方位，再按拼图块面积从小到大嵌套排列到输出网格中心。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中散布着若干个互不接触的拼图块，每个拼图块是一个正方形去掉一个角上的单像素后形成的 \"L 状缺角正方形\"（即边长为 S 的正方形共 S*S 个像素，去掉四个角之一的 1 个像素，剩余 S*S-1 个像素）。每个拼图块的主体用一种独特颜色填充，缺失角的对角位置上有一个不同颜色的单像素标记（该标记颜色在所有拼图块中相同，例如红色）。不同拼图块的边长 S 各不相同。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 识别每个拼图块的缺失角方位（左上、右上、左下、右下之一），缺失角是正方形边界上唯一为背景色的角。\n  - 确定目标统一方位：所有拼图块中出现最多的缺失角方位即为目标方位。\n  - 将每个缺失角方位不符合目标方位的拼图块旋转 90/180/270 度，使其缺失角转到目标方位。旋转时红色标记像素随主体一起旋转。\n  - 按拼图块边长从大到小排列：最大的拼图块居中放置，较小的拼图块依次叠放在其上方（以中心对齐），后放的覆盖先放的。\n  - 输出网格大小等于最大拼图块的边长。\n- `Key insight`：第一层推理是通过缺角位置和红色标记的空间关系确定每个块的方位和所需旋转；第二层推理是发现\"多数缺角方位\"决定统一目标方位的投票机制；第三层是按面积排序并嵌套叠放。三层结构中，投票机制最为隐蔽。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据彩色边框矩形内部灰色填充图案的对称性类型，从网格外部的变换图例中选取对应的替换图案，覆盖原有内部填充。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个由不同颜色边框围成的矩形区域，每个矩形内部填充着灰色像素构成的图案。这些灰色图案各自具有不同的对称性类型：有的关于垂直轴对称、有的关于水平轴对称、有的关于两轴都对称（即同时水平和垂直对称）、有的无任何对称性。网格的底部或右侧有一排变换图例，每个图例由一个对称性示意符号（用灰色像素画出的小型 \"I\"、\"-\"、\"+\" 或 \".\" 形状，分别代表垂直对称、水平对称、双轴对称、无对称）和紧邻的一个彩色小图案组成。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 分析每个边框矩形内部灰色图案的对称性类型（垂直/水平/双轴/无）。\n  - 在图例中找到对应对称性类型的示意符号。\n  - 用该图例中示意符号旁边的彩色小图案替换矩形内部的灰色填充：将彩色小图案平铺（tile）到矩形内部区域，裁剪到矩形边界。\n  - 边框颜色保持不变，图例区域保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：解题者必须先判断每个内部图案的对称性类别（需要空间推理而非计算），再将对称性类别映射到图例符号（需要理解符号的视觉含义），最后执行平铺替换。对称性分析和符号解读构成两层独立的归纳推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中彩色线段视为\"折叠指令\"，沿每条线段将其一侧的图案翻折到另一侧，翻折后的像素与原有像素按颜色混合规则叠加。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有一个由多种颜色组成的矩形图案区域。图案区域内部有一到两条由红色像素构成的水平或垂直直线段，每条线段完全横跨或纵跨图案区域。每条红色线段的一端标有一个绿色像素，指示\"被折叠\"的一侧（绿色像素所在的那一侧是被折过去的部分）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 按从外到内的顺序处理每条红色折叠线（若有两条，先处理离图案边缘更近的那条）。\n  - 对于每条折叠线，将绿色标记所在一侧的所有非红色、非绿色像素沿折叠线做镜像翻折到另一侧。\n  - 翻折后的像素覆盖目标位置：若目标位置为黑色，直接放置翻折像素的颜色；若目标位置已有非黑色像素，则保留原有颜色不变（原有像素优先）。\n  - 折叠完成后，擦除红色线段和绿色标记像素（变为黑色），同时擦除被折叠一侧的原始像素（它们已经翻折到另一侧）。\n  - 若翻折后像素超出原图案区域边界，则该像素被丢弃。\n- `Key insight`：绿色标记确定折叠方向（哪一侧被翻折），处理顺序（外到内）影响最终叠加结果。解题者需要先理解绿色标记的方向语义（第一层），再推断多次折叠的正确顺序及其叠加效果（第二层）。\n</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
